I would say if you are concerned about performance just store the last timestamp in a `static long` field and then make your comparisons against that. The class is unlikely to be unloaded that often while it is in use so the data would likely be 99% correct when tested.

I've created an interface and directed it towards a static method in `Blukon` like so:

```
   public static boolean isCollecting() {
        return false; // stub
        // use internal logic to decide if we are collecting something, if we return true here
        // then we will never get reset due to missed reading service restarts
    }
```
